      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "WIT WICKEE (6) disappointed backers last time out when fifth, beaten 17 metres, over 1720m at Young. Form prior to that was far better, including a sound second over 1730m at this track two starts ago. The recent run not a true indication. Good enough to win a race of this calibre. COHEN THE RED (7) has not raced for seven months. Looks forward enough for this return after winning in a recent trial. Sure to be right there at the finish. REDEMPTION MISS (2) was out of the money two runs ago then broke after suffering interference and finished seventh last start over 1660m at Parkes, arriving 11 metres behind the winner. Sure to enjoy an economical run from this much better draw. Won't find this any harder and she can bounce back to top-three form. MAJOR AUSTIN (9) has been about the mark of late and must be respected, the latest offering a sound second at Penrith over 1720m.",
